rew one tick after every other test had gone green.\n+- **Enough answers to boot.** `app_paths`, `fs_read_file` with an\n+  existing profile (bytes as a number array) and an id for each\n+  `plugin:event|listen` take startup through `ReactDOM.render` and\n+  `setupIpc`. Answer `fs_read_file` with a profile rather than an\n+  error: a missing one makes `State.load` build the default torrents,\n+  which fetches bundled assets. Keep every other command pending; a\n+  `null` from `get_engine_endpoint` starts the engine client's retry\n+  timers. Wrap the sandbox's `setInterval` and clear it afterwards,\n+  because startup's once-a-second `update` holds the process open.\n \n Anything asserted in the second mode runs on a later tick, so wrap it\n in a `process.on('unhandledRejection')` capture. `main.js`'s\n21:    \"test\": \"npm run lint && depcheck --ignores=standard,eslint,@babel/eslint-parser,madr,buffer,nightralph --ignore-dirs=build,build-vite,build-tauri,build-sidecar,dist && npm run test-unit\",\n85:    \"nightralph\": \"^0.0.56\",\npackage.json:21:    \"test\": \"npm run lint && depcheck --ignores=standard,eslint,@babel/eslint-parser,madr,buffer,nightralph --ignore-dirs=build,build-vite,build-tauri,build-sidecar,dist && npm run test-unit\",\npackage.json:85:    \"nightralph\": \"^0.0.56\",\npackage-lock.json:52:        \"nightralph\": \"^0.0.56\",\npackage-lock.json:8266:      \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/nightralph/-/nightralph-0.0.56.tgz\",\npackage-lock.json:8275:        \"nightralph\": \"dist/index.js\"\npackage-lock.json:18383:    \"nightralph\": {\npackage-lock.json:18385:      \"resolved\": \"https://registry.npmjs.org/nightralph/-/nightralph-0.0.56.tgz\",\nsrc/renderer/main.js:63:// No `catch`. There is no UI to report into at this point -- `onError`\nsrc/renderer/main.js:91:  if (err) return onError(err)\nsrc/renderer/main.js:337:  error: onError,\nsrc/renderer/main.js:375:  await Promise.all([\nsrc/renderer/main.js:376:    ipcOs.onLog((..