{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UgZ8PtcTgu1vj5WBm24MTz","type":"tool_result","content":"use std::fs;\nuse std::path::Path;\n\n// `bundle.resources` maps `../build-sidecar/` into the app's\n// `Contents/Resources`, and tauri-build checks that path during every\n// `cargo build` -- debug and release alike, because this build script\n// is what reads the config. But the directory is generated:\n// `bin/stage-sidecar.js` fills it from `beforeBundleCommand`, which the\n// Tauri CLI runs *after* the cargo build, and `bin/clean.js` deletes\n// it. A missing resource path is a hard error there, so without this a\n// clean checkout could not build the thing that generates it.\n//\n// Creating it empty is enough. A directory resource is walked, and a\n// walk that yields no files is skipped rather than failing, so a debug\n// build copies nothing. The bundler reads `../build-sidecar/` again\n// after `beforeBundleCommand` has filled it, so the packaged app still\n// gets the whole staged tree.\nfn main() {\n    let staging = Path::new(\"..\").join(\"build-sidecar\");\n    if let Err(err) = fs::create_dir_all(&staging) {\n        panic!(\"cannot create {}: {err}\", staging.display());\n    }\n\n    tauri_build::build()\n}\ndefault.json\n  }\n}\n\n// Listen to events from the main and webtorrent processes.\n//\n// Async, because every shim registration resolves to an unsubscribe\n// function (FR-10). The Electron implementation registers\n// synchronously before it resolves, but a non-Electron host is free\n// not to, so `ipcReady` -- which is what tells the main process the\n// renderer is listening -- waits for all of them. Nothing here is ever\n// unsubscribed: these listeners live as long as the window does, so\n// the returned unsubscribes are deliberately dropped.\nasync function setupIpc () {\n  const tc = controllers.torrent()\n\n  await Promise.all([\n    ipcOs.onLog((...args) => console.log(...args)),\n    ipcOs.onError((...args) => console.error(...args)),\n\n    ipcOs.onDispatch((...args) => dispatch(...args)),\n\n    ipcOs.onFullscreenChanged(onFullscreenChanged),\n    ipcOs.onWindowBoundsChanged(onWindowBoundsChanged),\n\n    ipcEngine.onTorrentParsed((...args) => tc.torrentParsed(...args)),\n    ipcEngine.onTorrentMetadata((...args) => tc.torrentMetadata(...args)),\n    ipcEngine.onTorrentDone((...args) => tc.torrentDone(...args)),\n    ipcEngine.onTorrentDone(() =>\n      controllers.torrentList().resumePausedTorrents()),\n    ipcEngine.onTorrentWarning((...args) => tc.torrentWarning(...args)),\n    ipcEngine.onTorrentError((...args) => tc.torrentError(...args)),\n\n    ipcEngine.onProgress((...args) => tc.torrentProgress(...args)),\n    ipcEngine.onFileModtimes((...args) => tc.torrentFileModtimes(...args)),\n    ipcEngine.onTorrentFileSaved((...args) => tc.torrentFileSaved(...args)),\n    ipcEngine.onAudioMetadata((...args) => tc.torrentAudioMetadata(...args)),\n    ipcEngine.onServerRunning((...args) => tc.torrentServerRunning(...args))\n  ])\n\n  await ipcOs.signalReady()\n\n  State.on('stateSaved', () => reportErrors(ipcOs.signalStateSaved()))\n}\n\n// Quits any modal popovers and returns to the torrent list screen\nfunction backToList () {\nsrc-tauri/src/main.rs:805:        if let Err(err) = app.emit(menu::CONTEXT_MENU_CLICK_EVENT, payload) {\nsrc-tauri/src/main.rs:957:    if let Err(err) = app.emit(DISPATCH_EVENT, payload) {\nsrc-tauri/src/main.rs:1377:    app.emit(cast::DEVICES_EVENT, session.devices())\nsrc-tauri/src/main.rs:1388:    app.emit(cast::DEVICES_EVENT, session.devices())\nsrc-tauri/src/main.rs:1498:    match read().and_then(|bounds| main.emit(window::BOUNDS_CHANGED_EVENT, bounds)) {\nsrc-tauri/src/main.rs:1526:            main.emit(window::FULLSCREEN_CHANGED_EVENT, fullscreen)?;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce4bfe32-bd95-4e29-ae29-d214b42a3e17","uuid":"d25708a0-fa95-48c3-a2f0-e5f37bdd63b5","timestamp":"2026-10-13T05:53:53.486Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"use std::fs;\nuse std::path::Path;\n\n// `bundle.resources` maps `../build-sidecar/` into the app's\n// `Contents/Resources`, and tauri-build checks that path during every\n// `cargo build` -- debug and release alike, because this build script\n// is what reads the config. But the directory is generated:\n// `bin/stage-sidecar.js` fills it from `beforeBundleCommand`, which the\n// Tauri CLI runs *after* the cargo build, and `bin/clean.js` deletes\n// it. A missing resource path is a hard error there, so without this a\n// clean checkout could not build the thing that generates it.\n//\n// Creating it empty is enough. A directory resource is walked, and a\n// walk that yields no files is skipped rather than failing, so a debug\n// build copies nothing. The bundler reads `../build-sidecar/` again\n// after `beforeBundleCommand` has filled it, so the packaged app still\n// gets the whole staged tree.\nfn main() {\n    let staging = Path::new(\"..\").join(\"build-sidecar\");\n    if let Err(err) = fs::create_dir_all(&staging) {\n        panic!(\"cannot create {}: {err}\", staging.display());\n    }\n\n    tauri_build::build()\n}\ndefault.json\n  }\n}\n\n// Listen to events from the main and webtorrent processes.\n//\n// Async, because every shim registration resolves to an unsubscribe\n// function (FR-10). The Electron implementation registers\n// synchronously before it resolves, but a non-Electron host is free\n// not to, so `ipcReady` -- which is what tells the main process the\n// renderer is listening -- waits for all of them. Nothing here is ever\n// unsubscribed: these listeners live as long as the window does, so\n// the returned unsubscribes are deliberately dropped.\nasync function setupIpc () {\n  const tc = controllers.torrent()\n\n  await Promise.all([\n    ipcOs.onLog((...args) => console.log(...args)),\n    ipcOs.onError((...args) => console.error(...args)),\n\n    ipcOs.onDispatch((...args) => dispatch(...args)),\n\n    ipcOs.o