{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfyiizvoyqfDyEQT1rvo7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found nothing worth fixing, and `.nightralph/findings.md` says \"No findings.\"\n\n**Spec coverage:**\n- **Shim:** `onLog` and `onError` are now standing subscriptions to the host's `log` and `error` events. They spread the payload and honour `{ once: true }`, the same way `onDispatch` does.\n- **Signals:** `signalReady` and `signalStateSaved` now call the new host commands `ipc_ready` and `state_saved`, and both resolve to `undefined`.\n- **Host:** the readiness record is in its own module, `src-tauri/src/ready.rs`, and is registered as managed state. Calling `ipc_ready` twice is not an error, and `state_saved` only acknowledges.\n- **Startup:** the `Promise.all` in `src/renderer/main.js:375` is unchanged. It now resolves, so the ready signal is sent and the state-saved hook is attached.\n- **Stub register:** it lost exactly the four names. Its comments now list only the two open dialogs for US-065 and no longer name a host log module.\n- **Tests:** the shim tests copy the existing `onDispatch` tests. The boot test checks that `ipc_ready` comes after the `log`, `error` and `dispatch` listeners are registered, and does not look at any banner text.\n\n**Checks I ran:** `npm test` passed all 4220 tests. In `src-tauri`, `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` were clean, and `cargo test` passed 209 tests. Clippy and `cargo test` only compile after `npm run build:tauri` has created `build-tauri`. That's a setup step, not a problem with this change.\n\n**Two small notes, not findings:**\n- `package.json` also adds `nightralph` to depcheck's ignore list. It was already a dependency, so this only keeps depcheck passing.\n- The shim spreads whatever the host sends. A future host that sends a single string on `log` would have it split into characters, and a non-array payload would throw. That is the convention the spec chose, and nothing on the host emits these events yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":331,"cache_read_input_tokens":52484,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":331},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce4bfe32-bd95-4e29-ae29-d214b42a3e17","uuid":"7b7054fd-4903-4915-8884-3d4ec821eafe","timestamp":"2026-10-13T05:55:58.312Z","request_id":"req_011CfyiizDQUG9JMzYiXukzu"}
